From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mac <xmachd@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/16] soc: qcom: geni-se: Allow a node without the DDR path

geni_icc_get() fails when a node lists interconnects but not the DDR
path. On the Oculus Quest 2 the QUP0 DDR path starts on a NoC that is
left as Android set it up, while SE4 still needs its qup-core and
qup-config votes. Leave the DDR path NULL in that case.

Also warn when there is no qup-core path: a register access without a
QUP core clock vote stalls the CPU.

Signed-off-by: mac <xmachd@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/qcom-geni-se.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom-geni-se.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom-geni-se.c
index 2fa6a4590..3f7b474f0 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom-geni-se.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom-geni-se.c
@@ -907,11 +907,33 @@ int geni_icc_get(struct geni_se *se, const char *icc_ddr)
 		if (!icc_names[i])
 			continue;
 
+		/*
+		 * A node may list only the register-access paths (qup-core,
+		 * qup-config), e.g. when the NoC the DDR path starts on is left
+		 * to the previous OS after kexec. The DDR path then stays NULL.
+		 */
+		if (i == GENI_TO_DDR &&
+		    of_property_match_string(se->dev->of_node,
+					     "interconnect-names",
+					     icc_names[i]) < 0) {
+			dev_info(se->dev, "no '%s' interconnect: no DDR vote\n",
+				 icc_names[i]);
+			continue;
+		}
+
 		se->icc_paths[i].path = devm_of_icc_get(se->dev, icc_names[i]);
 		if (IS_ERR(se->icc_paths[i].path))
 			goto err;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Without a qup-core path nothing here votes the QUP core clock, and a
+	 * register access while no other master holds that vote stalls the CPU.
+	 */
+	if (!se->icc_paths[GENI_TO_CORE].path)
+		dev_warn(se->dev,
+			 "no qup-core interconnect: QUP core clock not voted\n");
+
 	return 0;
 
 err:
